# Lantern — Moon Shrine, polished edition v3

A traveler pauses on a winding mountain stair below a moonlit shrine. Version 3 grounds the confirmed inner dark foreground tree and its mirrored partner with angular banks connected to the existing terrain. Their canopy shapes, placement and sway are unchanged. The previous upper-cliff ledges and smooth outer sky arch are retained unchanged; the composition, palette, motion and phase timing are preserved. This is a restrained revision of the earlier concept, retaining its composition, palette and clean, flat cut-paper style. All artwork is editable SVG geometry. There are no raster textures, grain, gradients, fonts, logos, loading text, progress UI or audio.

## Playable files

- `Lantern_E_MoonShrine_Polished_Preview.mp4` — complete 8-second presentation.
- `Lantern_E_MoonShrine_Polished_Intro.mp4` — 2-second opening, 120 frames.
- `Lantern_E_MoonShrine_Polished_Hold.mp4` — 4-second seamless loop, 240 frames.
- `Lantern_E_MoonShrine_Polished_Complete.mp4` — 2-second closing, 120 frames.

All four are 1920 × 1080, 60 fps, silent H.264/YUV420p with fast-start metadata. The preview joins the phases as 2/4/2 seconds. Frames are generated at their actual 1/60-second times, rather than repeating lower-rate frames.

## Editable source and resources

- `moon_shrine_master.svg`: editable vector still at hold phase zero.
- `render.py`: complete artwork, palette, animation functions, SVG generator and Cairo/librsvg renderer.
- `requirements.txt`: Python dependencies; no external art, font, network or account resources are needed.
- `rebuild.sh`: regenerate stills, all four production clips and verification results.
- `verify.py` / `verification.json`: technical checks, source-boundary equality, actual decoded motion and output format checks.
- `CHANGELOG.md`: the targeted v3 inner-foreground-pair correction.
- `verify_grounding.py` / `grounding_verification.json`: native rendered support checks beneath all 13 tree bases at all 240 hold frames, smooth-arch tangent check, and decoded transition/loop proofs.
- `verify_inner_roots.py` / `inner_root_verification.json`: continuous trunk-to-existing-terrain contact across all 240 hold frames and exact preservation of every other vector across all 480 preview frames.
- `preservation_reference.json`: v2 vector hashes used to prove the two banks are the only artwork change.
- `before_after_inner_roots.png`: decoded, native-resolution before/after crops of the confirmed pair.
- `decoded_inner_tree_contact.jpg`: both corrected roots across the entire encoded hold loop, including its last frame.
- `proof_01.png`, `contact_sheet.jpg`, `decoded_motion_contact.jpg`, `decoded_full_phase_proof.jpg`, `decoded_tree_grounding_proof.jpg`: additional review references, not runtime overlays. The last file shows the retained upper-cliff ledges.
- `manifest.json`: included file list and SHA-256 checksums. The manifest itself is excluded from its own checksum list.

The single SVG is a still. Full motion is defined by the editable paths and functions in `render.py`. Edit the `C` palette, shape functions or phase-dependent amplitudes. `svg_at(time_seconds, segment)` returns an independent SVG for the selected time; segments are `intro`, `hold` or `complete`.

## Playback / variable loading

Play Intro once, repeat Hold while loading, then play Complete at the next full hold boundary. The exact authored boundary poses match. Do not add a duplicate endpoint frame to the loop. The final color is `#11171f`. Waiting for a full hold boundary may add up to four seconds after readiness; arbitrary-phase completion would require a runtime adaptation.

These files are an animation source package. Unity integration, in-engine playback and runtime performance have not been tested.

## Rebuild locally

Requires Python 3, Pillow, NumPy, FFmpeg with libx264, Cairo, librsvg-2 and GLib/GObject. Debian-family system packages include `ffmpeg`, `libcairo2` and `librsvg2-2`. No download is performed by the rebuild script.

    python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
    ./rebuild.sh

Or run `python render.py --proof --all`, then `python verify.py`, `python verify_grounding.py` and `python verify_inner_roots.py`. For a smaller 960 × 540 draft, run `python render.py --draft`.

The renderer uses native shared libraries through Python ctypes. Encoding is deterministic in the included environment with a two-thread libx264 setup; different FFmpeg or library versions can produce different bytes while retaining the specified image and timing.

## Provenance

The original, polished-v1 and polished-v2 exports remain separate and unchanged. This folder contains new revision files; all scene artwork is procedural, with no third-party art assets.

## Visual grounding verification

Pixel support and continuous geometry are technical checks, not substitutes for visual judgment. The corrected pair was also reviewed against the user’s cropped reference, at full composition size and with enlarged encoded root crops. The new banks visibly join the existing foreground plane and bury the lower trunk ends without moving the canopy or adding isolated platforms.
